1	# notify-digest
     2	
     3	A small cron job that pulls a handful of feeds, filters the items per channel,
     4	and sends each channel a digest.
     5	
     6	## Running
     7	
     8	```sh
     9	cp config.example.toml config.toml
    10	python3 digest.py --config config.toml --db digest.sqlite3
    11	```
    12	
    13	`--dry-run` prints what would be sent instead of sending it.
    14	
    15	Requires Python 3.11+ (uses `tomllib`). No third-party dependencies.
    16	
    17	## Layout
    18	
    19	| File | Purpose |
    20	| --- | --- |
    21	| `digest.py` | CLI entry point, the per-run loop |
    22	| `feeds.py` | Fetching and normalising the three feed formats |
    23	| `store.py` | SQLite archive of everything seen |
    24	| `render.py` | Digest text |
    25	| `channels.py` | Delivery (stdout, webhook) |
    26	
    27	The `fixtures/` directory holds two snapshots of the feeds taken at different
    28	times, so you can work on this without network access. Point the config at
    29	`snapshot-a` or `snapshot-b`.
    30	
    31	## Deployment
    32	
    33	Runs from cron on the utility box:
    34	
    35	```
    36	*/15 * * * * cd /srv/notify-digest && python3 digest.py >> /var/log/digest.log 2>&1
    37	```
